, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Clarify whether `failover` activates purely by applies_to globs (config-only, matching the listed Scope) or ALSO by path-independent content tokens; if the latter, add the required registry.content_triggered_overlays code change to Scope and the ACs.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.332,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["registry.py content_triggered_overlays hardcodes triggers: `_CONCURRENCY_TOKENS` and the removed-decl scan; project trigger_tokens are read only via project_trigger_extensions for `.rebar/criteria_routing.json` overlays","search of packaged criteria_routing.json for 'trigger_tokens' returns no matches — no built-in overlay content-fires via config","Scope lists only registry OVERLAY_IDS + a routing entry with 'targeted fallback/retry/error-classification paths' (applies_to globs), no edit to content_triggered_overlays","The incident fix files failure.py/model_classes.py/tracing.py ARE covered by the named `**/llm/*.py` globs, so glob activation alone reaches them"],"finding":"The plan claims `failover` activates on `should_fall_back` / exception-translation code 'wired through the same registry mechanisms existing overlays use', but for a built-in OVERLAY_IDS member, path-independent CONTENT/token activation is not config-wireable — content_triggered_overlays hardcodes each built-in content trigger (_CONCURRENCY_TOKENS, the removed-declaration scan) and the trigger_tokens config path is reserved for PROJECT overlays only. Only glob activation (via applies_to) is achievable purely through the routing config the Scope lists.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f08c02b9ceba18619","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope — 'Activation is limited to ... should_fall_back / exception-translation style code wired through the same registry mechanisms existing overlays use.'","norm_id":"n91138eb692e1ce07","priority":0.268,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A fallback/classification change in a file NOT matching the failover globs (e.g. a should_fall_back predicate defined outside **/llm/) would silently never trigger the overlay, despite the plan implying content-based activation"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"State that `failover` is a glob-triggered overlay (applies_to = the retry/backoff/fallback/timeout/error-classification file globs, including **/llm/failure.py, **/llm/model_classes.py, **/llm/tracing.py) and drop the 'should_fall_back content wired through the same registry mechanisms' phrasing, since built-in content triggers are not config-wireable; OR, if content activation is required, add a scoped edit to registry.content_triggered_overlays with a committed failover token set plus a covering test.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State explicitly which registry mechanism activates `failover` on content-shaped `should_fall_back`/exception-translation code (glob `applies_to`, a hardcoded content-trigger token set in `content_triggered_overlays`, or base-reviewer escalation via the catalog entry), noting that packaged routing has no `trigger_tokens` field and glob `applies_to` matches paths only.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.601,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["registry.content_triggered_overlays fires a BUILT-IN overlay only from a HARDCODED token set (_CONCURRENCY_TOKENS at registry.py:417, _REMOVED_DECL_PATTERNS at registry.py:399) or a PROJECT overlay's trigger_tokens; packaged criteria_routing.json carries NO trigger_tokens field (search returned no matches).","glob_triggered_overlays (registry.py:340) matches applies_to globs against changed-file PATHS, not against 'should_fall_back'-style content, so a fallback edit whose translation code lives OUTSIDE the enumerated **/llm/failure.py, **/llm/model_classes.py, **/llm/tracing.py globs would not glob-fire.","The incident origin change 8fbd ('Enable class-scoped Anthropic fallback') is exactly the disposition-masking class this overlay must catch; if it edits a file outside the enumerated globs, activation would fall solely to base-reviewer escalation, which the plan lists only implicitly via the catalog entry."],"finding":"The activation mechanism for content-shaped 'should_fall_back'/exception-translation code is under-specified: the plan says it is 'wired through the same registry mechanisms existing overlays use' but does not name whether that is a glob applies_to, a content-trigger token set, or base-reviewer escalation — and glob applies_to matches file PATHS only.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2f15dac98fc4f932","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope, activation paragraph: 'should_fall_back / exception-translation style code wired through the same registry mechanisms existing overlays use'","norm_id":"n86f38e78ba05f96d","priority":0.099,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A retryable-primary-masking fallback is introduced in a module not matched by **/llm/*.py globs (e.g. a provider adapter or a project's own retry wrapper) and the overlay never glob-fires.","An author implements 'should_fall_back' content-triggering expecting a packaged trigger_tokens field that does not exist in the built-in routing schema."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Name the activation path: rely on the base-reviewer catalog entry for escalation on arbitrary-location fallback code, AND/OR add a hardcoded failover content-trigger token set (mirroring _CONCURRENCY_TOKENS: e.g. `should_fall_back`, `fallback_on`, `FallbackModel`, `except ... raise ... from`) to registry.content_triggered_overlays so the overlay fires on the diff content regardless of file path.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"3959f6b804a39c45","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["ee0f77ada49eb3e4",4122],"description_boxes":["399141be1d30ac26",0],"file_impact":["db92875b32c9